<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">13072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran's Revolutionary Guard says it struck United States bases on the soil of Jordan, Bahrain and Kuwait overnight, setting fuel and ammunition depots ablaze after American forces hit Iranian sites near the Strait of Hormuz.</s> <s>The war has crossed a threshold... it's no longer bilateral, because the moment US bases on third-country ground become targets, every Gulf state hosting American troops is exposed.</s> <s>Qatar has condemned the strikes, and Tehran now says its pledge of safe passage through Hormuz is over.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A twenty-five-year-old man set himself on fire outside a government office in Kathmandu and died, igniting protests inside Nepal's Parliament and on its streets.</s> <s>A public self-immolation is the sharpest possible signal of a citizen who felt he had no other channel, and the demand for an impartial probe points at institutions the young no longer trust.</s> <s>A five-member committee will investigate, as protesters call for the prime minister's resignation.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan says it's expelled two-point-five-nine million Afghans since twenty twenty-three, running the evictions through a dedicated foreign national security cell in Punjab.</s> <s>This is one of the largest forced-return operations of the decade — an entire bureaucracy of tracking and rolling quotas, sending families back to a country in economic collapse under Taliban rule.</s> <s>Residents are being urged to report undocumented Afghans, and the expulsions continue.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israel has set <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">27102026</say-as> for an election framed as a referendum on Benjamin Netanyahu.</s> <s>The coalition chose the latest date the law allows, buying the seventy-six-year-old premier months to reshape the war-and-security narrative before voters decide.</s> <s>A rival party led by Gadi Eisenkot now edges his Likud in polls, as Netanyahu also awaits a corruption verdict.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A fire tore through a packed Bangkok bar just after midnight, killing twenty-seven people who fled toward a single, flame-enveloped front door.</s> <s>That one-exit crush is the recurring mechanism in Southeast Asian nightlife fires, where lax enforcement turns a blaze into a mass-casualty event.</s> <s>Investigators haven't yet said whether the venue met Thailand's fire code.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Senator Lindsey Graham, a rare interventionist with direct access to the American president, died Saturday at seventy-one, hours after his tenth trip to Kyiv.</s> <s>He was, in effect, Ukraine's last advocate inside the president's ear, and no Republican holds equivalent sway.</s> <s>His death lands just as Congress weighs new sanctions on Russia.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Nearly nine-point-two million women — almost four in ten enrolled — have been struck from Maharashtra's flagship cash-transfer scheme after a state audit, most for failing identity verification.</s> <s>It exposes the tension at the heart of mass welfare politics — the loose enrolment that maximises votes also maximises leakage, and the poorest are caught in the gap.</s> <s>Officials say no money will be recovered except from men or the ineligible.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Ukraine's president is replacing his prime minister with Sergii Koretskyi, chief executive of the country's largest state oil-and-gas company, in a third wartime cabinet overhaul.</s> <s>Handing the premiership to an energy operator signals where Kyiv now believes its survival runs — fuel, revenue, and the drone-versus-refinery war over winter resilience.</s> <s>Parliament must approve the new cabinet before the grid comes under fresh attack.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A decade after an international tribunal rejected Beijing's claims to the South China Sea as baseless, the ruling still carries no enforcement, and China still refuses it.</s> <s>A third of the world's shipping crosses these waters, which makes the paralysis of that verdict a live test of whether international law binds a great power at all.</s> <s>Twelve nations reaffirmed the ruling this weekend, and Beijing called it a piece of waste paper.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Africa loses roughly eighty-eight-point-six billion dollars a year to corruption, about three-point-seven percent of the continent's output, by <sub alias="the U N Conference on Trade and Development">UNCTAD</sub>'s count.</s> <s>Civil-society groups meeting in Addis Ababa argue the problem is weak enforcement, not missing law — the statutes exist, the prosecutions don't.</s> <s>They've renewed calls for an International Anti-Corruption Court to pursue cases national courts won't touch.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>South Korea has issued its first-ever emergency heatwave alert under a new tiered system.</s> <s>The top tier triggers at a perceived thirty-eight degrees Celsius, or an actual thirty-nine, sustained for a full day — a threshold a temperate country rarely built its infrastructure to expect.</s> <s>Forecasters warn such alerts will grow more common as summer heat lengthens.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A seventeen-hundred-year pause in long-distance Pacific voyaging ended abruptly around the year nine hundred, and sediment isotopes now suggest why.</s> <s>A severe drought struck Samoa and Tonga just as their populations were growing, researchers found, pressure that may have pushed people back out across the ocean.</s> <s>The study can't yet resolve whether drought or better canoes mattered more.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Alzheimer's researchers gathered this week are pivoting away from amyloid, the protein that anchored decades of drug development but delivered only modest benefit.</s> <s>Attention is turning to tau and to the old bottleneck of crossing the blood-brain barrier, which has defeated neurological drugs for generations.</s> <s>New tau-targeted trial results, due later this year, will show whether reversal is even possible... in sha'Allah.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Researchers have described an artificial-intelligence system that detects malaria from blood smears without ever pooling patient data — each clinic trains locally and shares only the model's updates.</s> <s>Malaria's burden falls on low-resource clinics that can't legally or practically ship medical images to a central server, so this privacy-preserving design is what makes the tool deployable where it's actually needed.</s> <s>The team reports ninety-seven percent accuracy, though the work remains an early, unedited manuscript.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Brazil, labour prosecutors have documented a woman named Maria held in domestic servitude for fifty-five years, unpaid by three generations of a single family since she was seven.</s> <s>Prosecutors call it modern slavery — a reminder that bondage rarely announces itself, and often hides inside the ordinary rhythm of a household.</s> <s>The family agreed to a forty-thousand-dollar settlement, and Maria, now sixty-two, is still living with them.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>